  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8201.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8201.02 Scope. This chapter shall apply to situations, when in the line of duty, a law enforcement officer has been killed or injured, or is missing, there is sufficient information available regarding the law enforcement officer's last known location or physical description of an offender or vehicle involved, and the department determines that a public notification may aid in:\n\n(a) Apprehending a suspected offender who poses an imminent threat to the public or law enforcement personnel; or\n\n(b) Locating a missing law enforcement officer.\n\nSource. #13298, eff 11-30-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8200.html"
}
